---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageBack from '../components/PageBack.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const currentPath = Astro.url.pathname;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="What Digital Catholic is about — saint biographies and sacraments shared for knowledge and faith formation."
	currentPath={currentPath}
>
	<div class="page-content page-content--catalog">
		<PageBack href={withBase('/')} />
		<div class="catalog-prose">
		<h1>About Digital Catholic</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			Digital Catholic is a learning site dedicated to sharing the riches of the Catholic
			faith in a clear, accessible way.
		</p>

		<h2>What this site is about</h2>
		<p>
			We focus on two pillars of Catholic life: the <strong>biography of saints</strong> and
			the <strong>sacraments</strong>. Together they help us know who we are called to be and
			how God meets us in the Church.
		</p>

		<h2>Saints</h2>
		<p>
			The saints are our brothers and sisters in Christ who lived the Gospel with heroic love.
			Here you will find their stories—where they came from, what they endured, how they prayed,
			and what they teach us today. Their biographies are offered for knowledge and inspiration,
			so that their example can guide your own journey of faith.
		</p>

		<h2>Sacraments</h2>
		<p>
			The seven sacraments are visible signs of God’s invisible grace: Baptism, Confirmation,
			Eucharist, Penance, Anointing of the Sick, Holy Orders, and Matrimony. On this site we
			share teaching about each sacrament—what the Church believes, how they are celebrated, and
			why they are essential for every Catholic who seeks to know and live the faith.
		</p>

		<h2>Knowledge for sharing</h2>
		<p>
			Everything here is meant to be read, learned, and shared. Whether you are new to the
			faith, preparing for a sacrament, or deepening your devotion to the saints, Digital
			Catholic exists to make sound Catholic teaching available to all who wish to grow in
			understanding and love of Christ and His Church.
		</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
